# How much shorter can a prediction-powered interval be?

Paper and code for a study of confidence-interval width for the population mean when the labeled set, the
unlabeled set and the predictor are all fixed.

Layout of the delivery:

- `paper/`: LaTeX sources of the paper (main text, appendix, bibliography, impact and AI-disclosure statements, template files).
- `figures/`, `tables/`: every figure and table of the paper, as the paper includes them.
- `code/`: all code, environment and dependency versions, data acquisition, seeds, commands, expected run times,
  and which script produces which figure and table (`code/README.md`).
- `results/`: the per-cell results the figures and tables are computed from.
